workedExamples.question_text:
The graph of $f(x)=(x-2)^2-1$ is shown. Sketch (a) $y=|f(x)|$ and (b) $y=f(|x|)$. Label the zeros and turning points of each sketch.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (-0.8,0)--(4.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-2)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick,<->,domain=-0.4:4.4,samples=81] plot (\x,{(\x-2)*(\x-2)-1});
\node[black,below left] at (1,0) {$(1,0)$};
\node[black,below right] at (3,0) {$(3,0)$};
\node[black,below] at (2,-1) {$(2,-1)$};
\node[black,left] at (0,3) {$(0,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
(a) Keep the outer branches unchanged. Reflect the section between $x=1$ and $x=3$ upward. The zeros remain $(1,0)$ and $(3,0)$; they are local minima. The reflected turning point is a local maximum at $(2,1)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-0.8,0)--(4.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-1)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,dashed,domain=1:3,samples=41] plot (\x,{(\x-2)*(\x-2)-1});
\draw[curveBlue,thick,<-,domain=-0.4:1,samples=41] plot (\x,{(\x-2)*(\x-2)-1});
\draw[curveBlue,thick,domain=1:3,samples=41] plot (\x,{1-(\x-2)*(\x-2)});
\draw[curveBlue,thick,->,domain=3:4.4,samples=41] plot (\x,{(\x-2)*(\x-2)-1});
\node[black,below left] at (1,0) {$(1,0)$};
\node[black,below right] at (3,0) {$(3,0)$};
\node[black,above] at (2,1) {$(2,1)$};
\node[black,left] at (0,3) {$(0,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) Keep the part with $x\geq0$ and reflect it in the $y$-axis. The minima are $(-2,-1)$ and $(2,-1)$. The zeros are $(-3,0)$, $(-1,0)$, $(1,0)$ and $(3,0)$. The two halves meet at the local maximum $(0,3)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.8cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-4.5,0)--(4.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-2.2)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[curveBlue,thick,<-,domain=-4.4:0,samples=81] plot (\x,{(\x+2)*(\x+2)-1});
\draw[curveBlue,thick,->,domain=0:4.4,samples=81] plot (\x,{(\x-2)*(\x-2)-1});
\foreach \a in {-3,-1,1,3} {\draw[black] (\a,-0.08)--(\a,0.08);\node[black,below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\a,0) {$\a$};}
\node[black,below] at (-2,-1) {$(-2,-1)$};
\node[black,below] at (2,-1) {$(2,-1)$};
\node[black,above right] at (0,3) {$(0,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

